+# Senua AI patch, in design: with NEWTON_MPM_SWEPT_PROJECTION=1 (read once, here) project_outside_collider tests each
+# particle's step from its start (its position less its velocity over the step, as the particles are advected) against
+# the collider seen from there: a particle that set out outside a collider and whose travel along that side's normal
+# carries it past the surface is stopped at that surface. Only the step's end was tested, so a particle a step carries
+# across a wall thinner than its travel, or into the wall's far half, was let through (#4712's leak).
+_SWEPT_PROJECTION = os.environ.get("NEWTON_MPM_SWEPT_PROJECTION") == "1"
